WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.085 --> 00:00:13.996
One fall afternoon Mr.

2
00:00:14.036 --> 00:00:16.879
Harrison and Anne were having afternoon tea when Mr.

3
00:00:16.919 --> 00:00:20.723
Harrison inquired, "Been writing any more stories lately, Anne?"

4
00:00:22.545 --> 00:00:24.788
"No," answered Anne rather curtly.

5
00:00:25.852 --> 00:00:32.135
"I heard that someone recently sent a big envelope to the Rollings Reliable Baking Company in Montreal," remarked

6
00:00:32.215 --> 00:00:32.996
Mr. Harrison.

7
00:00:33.016 --> 00:00:38.818
"I thought maybe it was you, sending in your story to the Rollings Reliable Story Competition."

8
00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.219
"I would never do that!"

9
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:43.140
replied Anne indignantly.

10
00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:50.044
"I read about the competition, but I think it's disgraceful to write a story to advertise a baking

11
00:00:50.124 --> 00:00:53.081
powder. It's almost as bad as Mr.

12
00:00:53.141 --> 00:00:55.761
Parker's fence with advertising all over it!"

13
00:00:57.322 --> 00:01:00.843
When Anne said that, she had no idea of how the day would unfold.

14
00:01:01.823 --> 00:01:04.824
That very evening, Diana popped into Green Gables.

15
00:01:05.584 --> 00:01:06.704
She was carrying a letter.

16
00:01:06.724 --> 00:01:09.945
"Anne, open this letter right away!"

17
00:01:10.365 --> 00:01:11.346
she said excitedly.

18
00:01:11.366 --> 00:01:14.286
"I was at the post office, so I picked it up for you.

19
00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:16.987
I have a feeling it's good news."

20
00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:19.828
Puzzled, Anne opened the letter.

21
00:01:20.576 --> 00:01:22.297
"Dear Madam," she read.

22
00:01:22.317 --> 00:01:30.099
"We take much pleasure in informing you that your charming story 'Averil's Atonement' has won the first prize

23
00:01:30.139 --> 00:01:33.420
of $25 in our recent story competition.

24
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:37.681
Regards, Rollings Reliable Baking Company.

25
00:01:38.881 --> 00:01:41.422
I don't understand," said Anne blankly.

26
00:01:42.483 --> 00:01:43.723
Diana clapped her hands.

27
00:01:43.743 --> 00:01:46.044
"Oh, I knew it would win the prize!

28
00:01:46.364 --> 00:01:47.144
I was sure of it.

29
00:01:48.008 --> 00:01:50.329
I sent your story into the competition, Anne."

30
00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:52.531
"Diana Barry!"

31
00:01:52.971 --> 00:01:53.771
Anne exclaimed.

32
00:01:54.772 --> 00:02:00.055
Diana was not always the most observant person, but she realized that Anne was not overjoyed.

33
00:02:00.075 --> 00:02:02.797
"Why, Anne, you don't seem a bit pleased."

34
00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.299
Anne instantly made herself smile.

35
00:02:06.319 --> 00:02:12.522
"Diana," Anne began, "of course I'm touched that you helped me get my story published.

36
00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:21.365
That was very unselfish of you, but there wasn't a word in my story about about Anne choked

37
00:02:21.425 --> 00:02:23.966
a little over the word, "baking powder!"

38
00:02:23.986 --> 00:02:26.747
"Oh, I put that in," said Diana.

39
00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:29.568
"It was easy!

40
00:02:30.228 --> 00:02:32.128
You know the scene where Averil makes the cake?

41
00:02:33.089 --> 00:02:37.810
Well, I just added in that she used Rollings Reliable Baking Powder, and that's why the cake was

42
00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:38.350
so delicious.

43
00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:43.411
And in the final scene, after Averil and Harold kiss "Yes?"

44
00:02:44.072 --> 00:02:45.132
said Anne quietly.

45
00:02:46.644 --> 00:02:52.288
"I wrote, 'and they always used Rollings Reliable Baking Powder in every cake, and lived happily ever after,'"

46
00:02:52.648 --> 00:02:53.889
Diana quoted proudly.

47
00:02:53.909 --> 00:02:59.313
"Oh," gasped Anne, as if someone had thrown cold water on her.

48
00:02:59.333 --> 00:03:04.156
"And you've won twenty-five dollars," continued Diana jubilantly.

49
00:03:04.176 --> 00:03:08.659
"Why, I heard that magazines only pay five dollars a story!

50
00:03:08.679 --> 00:03:10.801
I'm so happy for you, Anne."

51
00:03:12.102 --> 00:03:14.984
Anne held the hateful check that had been attached to the letter.

52
00:03:15.964 --> 00:03:17.606
"I can't take it, Diana.

53
00:03:18.427 --> 00:03:22.370
You deserve it, since you sent the story in and made the changes.

54
00:03:22.390 --> 00:03:25.393
I I wouldn't have sent it."

55
00:03:25.413 --> 00:03:27.615
"Absolutely not!

56
00:03:28.436 --> 00:03:30.678
I would never take that money; it's yours, Anne!

57
00:03:31.579 --> 00:03:35.522
The honor of being a friend of the prizewinner is enough for me," Diana said.

58
00:03:37.124 --> 00:03:41.328
Anne suddenly bent forward, put her arms around Diana, and kissed her cheek.

59
00:03:42.532 --> 00:03:46.854
"I think you are the sweetest and truest friend in the world, Diana.

60
00:03:47.574 --> 00:03:48.274
Thank you."

61
00:03:49.355 --> 00:03:51.036
Anne left with tears in her eyes.

62
00:03:52.076 --> 00:03:55.617
She felt deeply embarrassed over what had happened to her literary endeavor.

63
00:03:55.637 --> 00:03:59.639
"I will never live this down," she thought.

64
00:03:59.659 --> 00:04:05.481
"Never!" A week later Anne left for Halifax.

65
00:04:06.482 --> 00:04:11.264
For the first time, she was not sorry to leave Avonlea because her last week there had not

66
00:04:11.304 --> 00:04:11.964
been pleasant.

67
00:04:12.884 --> 00:04:18.249
Her story was published in all the newspapers on Prince Edward Island, and everyone had an opinion.

68
00:04:19.229 --> 00:04:22.812
Josie Pye was sure that Anne had copied the story while Mrs.

69
00:04:22.892 --> 00:04:28.457
Lynde said, unimpressed, "It's perfectly amazing, the price they pay for such lies!"

70
00:04:30.479 --> 00:04:36.404
Back in Halifax Anne, Priscilla, Stella, and Phil settled quickly into their new home at Patty's Place.

71
00:04:37.416 --> 00:04:42.619
Mrs. Lynde and Marilla had given Anne jams and cakes and other foods, so the girls had a

72
00:04:42.679 --> 00:04:43.380
full pantry.

73
00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.282
And soon they were welcoming visitors.

74
00:04:47.322 --> 00:04:52.806
They passed many enjoyable Friday evenings entertaining guests around the fireplace in their cozy living room.

75
00:04:54.207 --> 00:04:58.809
Gilbert was a frequent visitor, but Anne still felt uncomfortable around him at times.

76
00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.612
It seemed as if their relationship had gotten very complicated.

77
00:05:03.852 --> 00:05:09.294
One afternoon Anne was sitting under the apple tree behind Patty's Place when she saw Gilbert coming toward

78
00:05:09.334 --> 00:05:10.835
her with a bunch of wildflowers.

79
00:05:10.855 --> 00:05:15.497
"Don't these remind you of home and our old school picnics, Anne?"

80
00:05:15.817 --> 00:05:16.337
he asked.

81
00:05:17.858 --> 00:05:20.259
Anne smiled and buried her face in the flowers.

82
00:05:20.279 --> 00:05:23.640
"I feel like I'm back in Avonlea right now!"

83
00:05:23.660 --> 00:05:27.121
"Will you go back to Avonlea for winter vacation?"

84
00:05:27.422 --> 00:05:28.162
Gilbert asked.

85
00:05:28.182 --> 00:05:31.043
"Yes, I will," Anne answered.

86
00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:33.064
"And I guess you will too?"

87
00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:36.941
"No, I'll be working in Halifax," said Gilbert.

88
00:05:36.961 --> 00:05:39.923
"Oh," said Anne, surprised.

89
00:05:40.883 --> 00:05:44.865
She couldn't picture what a whole Avonlea winter would be like without Gilbert.

90
00:05:44.885 --> 00:05:52.708
"Well, a new job that's exciting," said Anne, without any very clear idea of what she was saying.

91
00:05:53.648 --> 00:05:56.429
Gilbert was now staring at Anne with a strange expression.

92
00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:00.331
Anne wished desperately that Phil would come out and interrupt them.

93
00:06:00.351 --> 00:06:07.615
"Well uh I found a cluster of white violets under that old twisted tree today," Anne mumbled.

94
00:06:07.635 --> 00:06:11.998
"They were so pretty, I felt as if I'd discovered a gold mine!"

95
00:06:12.019 --> 00:06:16.822
"You are always discovering gold mines, Anne," said Gilbert.

96
00:06:17.702 --> 00:06:19.043
"Let's find some more violets.

97
00:06:20.024 --> 00:06:23.246
I think I saw some more over there," suggested Anne quickly.

98
00:06:23.266 --> 00:06:30.612
"I'll call Phil and—" "Never mind Phil and the violets just now, Anne," said Gilbert, quietly taking her

99
00:06:30.652 --> 00:06:33.433
hand. He looked deep into Anne's eyes.

100
00:06:33.453 --> 00:06:35.654
"There is something I want to say to you."

101
00:06:35.674 --> 00:06:39.457
"Oh, don't say it," cried Anne.

102
00:06:39.477 --> 00:06:42.799
"Don't please, Gilbert," she begged him.

103
00:06:42.819 --> 00:06:45.741
"I must," Gilbert said firmly.

104
00:06:45.761 --> 00:06:48.802
"Things can't go on like this any longer.

105
00:06:49.743 --> 00:06:50.724
Anne, I love you.

106
00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:52.284
You know I do.

107
00:06:53.325 --> 00:06:54.566
I can't tell you how much.

108
00:06:55.506 --> 00:06:57.908
Will you promise me that one day you'll be my wife?"
